  "description": "Link-Local Multicast Name Resolution (LLMNR) is a secondary name resolution \nprotocol. With LLMNR, queries are sent using multicast over a local network link on a single subnet from a client computer to another client computer on the same subnet that also has LLMNR enabled. LLMNR does not require a DNS server or DNS client configuration and provides name resolution in scenarios in which conventional DNS name resolution is not possible.\n\nThe recommended state for this setting is: Enabled",
